.TITLE "ps"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays information about the currently running processes. It provides a __snapshot__ of system activity, showing which programs are active and how many __resources__ they are using.

.DIV "TLDR"
**ps**
Displays a list of processes running in the current terminal session.
> 

**ps -e**
Displays every process currently running on the entire system.
> __-e__ every process flag

**ps -f**
Displays a full-format listing, including the parent process ID and start time.
> __-f__ full format flag

**ps -u user**
Displays all processes owned by a specific user.
> __-u__ user flag | __user__ the target username

**ps -e --forest**
Displays processes in a tree-like hierarchy to show parent-child relationships.
> __-e__ every process | __--forest__ tree display flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combining flags like __ps -e -f__ is the most common way to get a comprehensive view of all system activity. If you need to find a specific process, pipe the output to grep (e.g., __ps -e -f | grep "name"__).

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:top** **linux:kill**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/ps.1.html__
